{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01UnVwMFZuZyjHFEaQy9P1Kz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Root Cause Analysis Complete\n\n### Issue: \"the mummer\" merged with \"Prince Prospero\"\n\n**Symptom:** \"the mummer\" appears as an alias of \"the Prince Prospero\"\n\n**Data flow trace:**\n1. Appears in: `analysis.json` character list\n2. Stored in: `AnalysisResult.characters[0].aliases`\n3. Generated by: `CharacterConsensusBuilder.build()` at line 394 (cross-group resolution)\n4. **Originates in:** `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py:_llm_cross_group_resolution():2114-2131`\n\n**Root cause:** The context snippets provided to the LLM for cross-group resolution are too short to capture the confrontation scene. Poe writes very long sentences - the confrontation happens in a single ~500-character sentence. But the code only provides:\n- 4 contexts of max 150 chars for epithets (line 2116)\n- 3 contexts of max 120 chars for proper names (line 2129)\n\nThe confrontation detection code at line 2168 runs AFTER the LLM has already decided to merge them, but by then it's too late - the LLM didn't see enough context to realize they're separate entities.\n\n**Confidence:** HIGH\n\n## Phase 2: Implement Fix\n\nThe fix is to increase the context window size specifically for cross-group resolution so the LLM can see the full confrontation scene:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":683,"cache_read_input_tokens":64883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":683,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"337a36e3-d70d-45be-ab91-b299e97b48c7","uuid":"22fa6dc6-0f25-45a6-bfe5-d93e212ee7fe"}
