{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01W3rJy4XGbiwVsuGgD7ah8B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The analysis is running in the background. While it runs, let me document my findings so far:\n\n## Root Cause Analysis Documentation\n\n### Issue: False character merge: \"the mummer\" merged with Prince Prospero\n\n**Symptom:** \"the mummer\" appears as an alias of \"the Prince Prospero\" in the character list\n\n**Data flow trace:**\n1. Appears in: `output/masque_of_red_death/analysis.json` character list\n2. Stored in: `AnalysisResult.characters[0].aliases = [\"the mummer\"]`\n3. Generated by: `CharacterConsensusBuilder.build()` at line 394-404 (cross-group resolution merge)\n4. **Originates in:** `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py:_llm_cross_group_resolution():2114-2131`\n\n**Root cause:** The context snippets provided to the LLM for cross-group resolution were too short (150 chars for epithets, 120 chars for proper names) to capture Poe's long confrontation sentence (~500 characters). The LLM couldn't see that \"the mummer\" confronts and kills \"Prince Prospero\", so it incorrectly merged them.\n\nThe confrontation detection code at line 2168 does exist and would block the merge, but it only runs AFTER the LLM has already decided. The LLM prompt explicitly warns against merging entities in confrontation (lines 109-111 and 123), but the LLM couldn't apply this rule without seeing enough context.\n\n**Confidence:** HIGH\n\n**Fix applied:** Increased context window from 150→400 chars for epithets and 120→400 chars for proper names in cross-group resolution (lines 2116, 2131)\n\nLet me check the smoke test progress:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":489,"cache_read_input_tokens":70090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":489,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"contex